  "slug": "end-structural-df64",
  "summary": "Preprints pair H&E models with mIF, spatial proteomics and Xenium supervision while testing scanner and cross-dataset robustness of pathology models.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is anchoring histology-based models to measurable molecular or cell-level reference data and checking whether outputs survive changes in acquisition. HERMES applies a process reward that verifies stated quantities against cell-level truth from paired mIF. VirTues-M2 jointly pretrains on H&E morphology and spatial proteomics, and XenoType supervises H&E cell-type classification with paired Xenium and scRNA-seq references. On the robustness side, a tempering and few-shot calibration method targets slide-scanner dependence of digital biomarkers, and a YOLO-Swin white blood cell pipeline reports cross-dataset macro-F1 of 0.879. The items are heterogeneous in task, but the new element is the pairing of molecular supervision or verifiable reasoning with explicit reproducibility evaluation. All are preprints, so findings remain provisional.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
